<p>Decimal 36867. Default value: 174. Also known as <strong>VICCR3</strong>.</p>
<p>This register has three functions:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Bit 7</strong> - bit 0 of the raster line counter, the low bit that does not fit
in VIC_RASTERLINE ($9004).</li>
<li><strong>Bits 6-1</strong> - the number of character rows the chip draws. Normally 23.</li>
<li><strong>Bit 0</strong> - character height: 0 gives 8x8 characters, 1 gives 8x16 double
height characters (used by Vic Bitmap Mode).</li>
</ul>
<p>The row count sits in bits 6-1, so a row count has to be doubled before it is
written, and bit 7 must be preserved:</p>
<code>
// draw 20 rows of 8x8 characters
SCREEN_TEXT_HEIGHT := (SCREEN_TEXT_HEIGHT &amp; 128) + (20 * 2);
</code>
